PURPOSE Reconstruct executable plans and export paper-method routes and metrics.
INPUT arc solutions or integral route selections, catalog, case and configuration
OUTPUT validated Plan, route/metric tables and solver/search records
REFERENCES Program.Generating_Results/Generating_Master_Results;
           Generating_TS_RS_results; Y_to_notation; GeneratingRoutes

PROCEDURE ReconstructPlan(pool,weights,input,config)
    IF any route weight is outside integer tolerance
        record reason=fractional; return none
    REQUIRE exactly one selected physical route per vehicle, including unused
    REQUIRE exactly one complete selected package route per order, including unserved
    obtain ordered original arc records from selected routes
    join stored package fragments at identical transfer location/time
    assignments := ReconstructCarriers(vehiclePaths,packagePaths,input,config)
    IF no consistent assignments exist: record support diagnostic; return none
    acceptedOrders := orders with a complete physically served package path
    unservedOrders := orders whose selected package route is the unserved choice
    cost := etaK*sum(selected vehicle path costs)
          + etaR*sum(selected package path costs)
    plan := Plan{vehiclePaths,packagePaths,assignments,acceptedOrders,
                 unservedOrders,cost,modelIdentity,status:reconstructed,input}
    IF ValidatePlan(plan,input,config): return plan
    return none with validation report

PROCEDURE ReconstructCarriers(vehiclePaths,packagePaths,input,config)
    FOR each selected supported package arc (r,a)
        enumerate selected compatible vehicle arcs by full endpoint/state/time key
        create binary carrier[k,r,a] only for compatible physical vehicles
        require sum(k) carrier[k,r,a] = 1
    FOR each vehicle movement/handling/waiting state transition
        require total assigned package load <= that vehicle's Cp
    keep carrier continuity between adjacent package arcs unless a legal
        transfer state/time permits a carrier change
    preserve onboard/current-carrier commitments supplied by input.dynamicState
    solve this finite assignment-feasibility problem with zero objective
    return assignments if feasible, otherwise none

PROCEDURE ValidatePlan(plan,input=plan.input,config=input.configuration)
    IF plan is none: return false with reason=no_plan
    FOR each physical vehicle path and served package path
        CheckPath(path,its source,its sink,config)
    verify one route choice per physical vehicle and per complete order
    verify visible orders, pickup-before-delivery, windows and allowed transfer sites
    verify carrier support/capacity on every supported package arc and transition
    verify every paper service-incidence and coupling row from the selected records
    verify vehicle duty limits, mode/zone restrictions and declared LT schedules
    REQUIRE unserved orders use only their declared penalty choice
    REQUIRE previously accepted unfinished orders remain physically served
    IF input.dynamicState exists: CheckCommitments(plan,input.dynamicState)
    recomputedCost := etaK*sum(vehicle arc costs)+etaR*sum(package arc costs)
    REQUIRE abs(recomputedCost-plan.cost) <= configured objective tolerance
    return valid or failure diagnostics

PROCEDURE ExportArcSolution(solution,network,caseId)
    REQUIRE solution.plan exists and passes ValidatePlan
    FOR each physical owner
        emit ordered endpoints,times,original arc IDs,vehicle type and arc costs
    emit complete package paths, carrier assignments and transfer location/time
    emit unserved choices separately from physical service
    emit recomputed objective, status, case/config/catalog identifiers

PROCEDURE ExportMasterSolution(pool,weights,input,config)
    emit selected route IDs,physical ownership,weights,arcs and unweighted costs
    IF weights are fractional
        label output=LP mixture; return tables without an executable Plan
    plan := ReconstructPlan(pool,weights,input,config)
    return tables,plan and validation report

PROCEDURE ComputeServiceMetrics(plan,orders)
    denominator := eligible submitted orders in the declared epoch/case
    completed := orders whose required physical delivery events have occurred
    plannedServed := plan.acceptedOrders
    transfer := served orders changing carrier at a legal matching transfer state
    shared := served orders overlapping another load on a physical carrier
    return separate planned/completed counts and ratios with their denominator
    report vehicle cost,package cost,unserved penalty and weighted objective

PROCEDURE FormatRoute(path)
    map service roles to readable labels; retain original IDs/times in data columns
    return notation and path-validation status

PROCEDURE ExportSearchHistory(nodes,iterations)
    emit node/parent IDs,branch decisions,objective,status and stop reason
    include a bound only with its supplied scope and certificate
    return ordered history

NOTES
    A Plan requires carrier reconstruction and network/coupling validation.
    Validation covers zero-time cycles, unserved choices, onboard work and cost
    weights applied once. Experiment and example outputs retain their own case
    identifiers and configurations.
